# CastSpell's own PayManaCost call handles a two-colour cost the same as
# paymanacost always has -- Armored Wolf-Rider ({3}{G}{W}) auto-pays its one
# green and one white pip straight from the pool (Pool.Pay's own colour
# matching), leaving three mana (2 green, 1 white) to answer the generic
# amount through queue paygeneric, same as every other CastSpell fixture's
# single-colour cost.
startturn human
advance 3
tapformana human 2 G
tapformana human 3 G
tapformana human 4 G
tapformana human 5 W
tapformana human 6 W
queue paygeneric G
queue paygeneric G
queue paygeneric W
castspell human 1
resolvestack
